{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function replayRunStream<TOffset>(\n   durability, \n   offset?, \nsignal?): AsyncGenerator<AGUIEvent>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/stream-durability.ts#L588","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/stream-durability.ts:588"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replay a run's delivery-durability log as a bare stream of chunks, for\ncallers that serve a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"joinRun"},{"type":"text","value":" handler without an HTTP "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":" — e.g. a\nTanStack Start server function returning an async iterable:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"async function* joinImageRun({ data: runId }: { data: string }) {\n  yield* replayRunStream(memoryStream({ runId }))\n}\n\n// Serve it from a server function whose handler is the generator above\n// (`createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).inputValidator(...)`).","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NOTE: the example deliberately declares the generator separately instead of\ninlining it into the server-fn builder chain. TanStack Start's server-fn\nVite plugin decides whether a module needs compiling by regex-matching the\nSOURCE for a dotted "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handler("},{"type":"text","value":" call, and JSDoc survives into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":" — an\ninlined chain here would make every Start app treat this package as a\nserver-fn module and try to resolve its framework's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/*-start"},{"type":"text","value":"\npackage, failing the build wherever that framework is not the one installed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"offset"},{"type":"text","value":" (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'-1'"},{"type":"text","value":" — from the start) and tails until the\nproducer closes the log or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal"},{"type":"text","value":" aborts, exactly like the HTTP\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumeServerSentEventsResponse"},{"type":"text","value":" path."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toffset","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TOffset"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOffset"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"durability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"durability"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/StreamDurability.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamDurability"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOffset"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"offset","children":[{"type":"text","value":"offset?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOffset"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"signal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"signal?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortSignal"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AsyncGenerator"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AGUIEvent.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGUIEvent"}]},{"type":"text","value":">"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"toffset","text":"TOffset","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"durability","text":"durability","level":3},{"id":"offset","text":"offset?","level":3},{"id":"signal","text":"signal?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction replayRunStream<TOffset>(\n   durability, \n   offset?, \nsignal?): AsyncGenerator<AGUIEvent>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/stream-durability.ts:588](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/stream-durability.ts#L588)\n\nReplay a run's delivery-durability log as a bare stream of chunks, for\ncallers that serve a `joinRun` handler without an HTTP `Response` — e.g. a\nTanStack Start server function returning an async iterable:\n\n```ts\nasync function* joinImageRun({ data: runId }: { data: string }) {\n  yield* replayRunStream(memoryStream({ runId }))\n}\n\n// Serve it from a server function whose handler is the generator above\n// (`createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).inputValidator(...)`).\n```\n\nNOTE: the example deliberately declares the generator separately instead of\ninlining it into the server-fn builder chain. TanStack Start's server-fn\nVite plugin decides whether a module needs compiling by regex-matching the\nSOURCE for a dotted `handler(` call, and JSDoc survives into `dist` — an\ninlined chain here would make every Start app treat this package as a\nserver-fn module and try to resolve its framework's `@tanstack/*-start`\npackage, failing the build wherever that framework is not the one installed.\n\nReads from `offset` (default `'-1'` — from the start) and tails until the\nproducer closes the log or `signal` aborts, exactly like the HTTP\n`resumeServerSentEventsResponse` path.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TOffset\n\n`TOffset` *extends* `string`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### durability\n\n[`StreamDurability`](../interfaces/StreamDurability.md)\\<`TOffset`\\>\n\n### offset?\n\n`TOffset`\n\n### signal?\n\n`AbortSignal`\n\n## Returns\n\n`AsyncGenerator`\\<[`AGUIEvent`](../type-aliases/AGUIEvent.md)\\>\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: replayRunStream\ntitle: replayRunStream\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction replayRunStream<TOffset>(\n   durability, \n   offset?, \nsignal?): AsyncGenerator<AGUIEvent>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/stream-durability.ts:588](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/stream-durability.ts#L588)\n\nReplay a run's delivery-durability log as a bare stream of chunks, for\ncallers that serve a `joinRun` handler without an HTTP `Response` — e.g. a\nTanStack Start server function returning an async iterable:\n\n```ts\nasync function* joinImageRun({ data: runId }: { data: string }) {\n  yield* replayRunStream(memoryStream({ runId }))\n}\n\n// Serve it from a server function whose handler is the generator above\n// (`createServerFn({ method: 'GET' }).inputValidator(...)`).\n```\n\nNOTE: the example deliberately declares the generator separately instead of\ninlining it into the server-fn builder chain. TanStack Start's server-fn\nVite plugin decides whether a module needs compiling by regex-matching the\nSOURCE for a dotted `handler(` call, and JSDoc survives into `dist` — an\ninlined chain here would make every Start app treat this package as a\nserver-fn module and try to resolve its framework's `@tanstack/*-start`\npackage, failing the build wherever that framework is not the one installed.\n\nReads from `offset` (default `'-1'` — from the start) and tails until the\nproducer closes the log or `signal` aborts, exactly like the HTTP\n`resumeServerSentEventsResponse` path.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TOffset\n\n`TOffset` *extends* `string`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### durability\n\n[`StreamDurability`](../interfaces/StreamDurability.md)\\<`TOffset`\\>\n\n### offset?\n\n`TOffset`\n\n### signal?\n\n`AbortSignal`\n\n## Returns\n\n`AsyncGenerator`\\<[`AGUIEvent`](../type-aliases/AGUIEvent.md)\\>\n"}
